        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-01T07:37:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think this is necessary. This doesn\u0027t test the request ; it tests that the telephony network agent can set the access UIDs on the network in the right conditions.\n\nAs I understand it, it\u0027s fine for the telephony factory to set the service package as having access to any of its restricted networks if it wants to. For example, I think it should be fine to give it access to the IMS network.\n\nI added comments here to clarify the current behavior. If you think we should restrict this more, then I\u0027m happy to change it to only permit the factory to give access to the CBS network. Then I\u0027ll need one more line in the check in NetworkAgentInfo.\n\nPlease let me know what you think.",
      "parentUuid": "542bbd50_660e1e22",
